rjg|n|Cessation of supply, or total defect; a failing; deficiency; as, failure of rain; failure of crops. ; Omission; nonperformance; as, the failure to keep a promise. ; Want of success; the state of having failed. ; Decay, or defect from decay; deterioration; as, the failure of memory or of sight. ; A becoming insolvent; bankruptcy; suspension of payment; as, failure in business. ; A failing; a slight fault.	a:be7,96,9;28io,88,3;1myz,52,5;19nf,45,5;24t4,41,3;1m14,36,4;efl,35,9;xxl,22,2;1lw4,9,3~efl,35,9;be7,96,9;1myz,52,5;19nf,45,5;1m14,36,4;1lw4,9,3;24t4,41,3;28io,88,3;xxl,22,2	v:1thb,4,4~1thb,4,4	V:1bhw,67,2;1ess,57,5~1ess,57,5;1bhw,67,2	n:xks,53,9;1m4i,35,11;xxl,28,3;138,27,3;1n1i,24,31;rnc,20,3~1n1i,24,31;1m4i,35,11;xks,53,9;rnc,20,3;xxl,28,3;138,27,3	N:1bhw,96,15;1bgu,65,22;1pn7,60,5;1l9d,42,11;1pn1,36,5;1ess,34,1;1l91,28,14~1bgu,65,22;1bhw,96,15;1l91,28,14;1l9d,42,11;1pn7,60,5;1pn1,36,5;1ess,34,1
