rvm|a|Full of favor; favoring; manifesting partiality; kind; propitious; friendly. ; Conducive; contributing; tending to promote or facilitate; advantageous; convenient. ; Beautiful; well-favored.	e:1c22,41,5~1c22,41,5
rvt|n|A person or thing regarded with peculiar favor; one treated with partiality; one preferred above others; especially, one unduly loved, trusted, and enriched with favors by a person of high rank or authority. ; Short curls dangling over the temples; -- fashionable in the reign of Charles II. ; The competitor (as a horse in a race) that is judged most likely to win; the competitor standing highest in the betting.	a:hp5,33,2~hp5,33,2
rvt|a|Regarded with particular affection, esteem, or preference; as, a favorite walk; a favorite child.	j:1uoy,65,9;20bq,55,3;22fi,46,2;1p0j,9,3~1uoy,65,9;20bq,55,3;1p0j,9,3;22fi,46,2
